; DOMAIN: arithmetic-theta [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-25]
; Claim: The Kudla-Millson arithmetic theta lift produces a theta form valued in the arithmetic Chow group CH-hat of an orthogonal/unitary Shimura variety, whose generating series sum_T Z-hat(T) q^T is a (nonholomorphic) modular form of weight n/2+1 with coefficients arithmetic special-cycle classes. This is the arithmetic companion completing the special-cycle program: it lifts the geometric Borcherds realization (146) and the global Kudla generating series (144) to arithmetic Chow groups, with Kudla-Rapoport (145) local densities computing its archimedean and non-archimedean heights, and specializes to GKZ (143) in weight 3/2. Bridge: genesis_borcherds_lift (geometric divisor realization it lifts to CH-hat) + genesis_kudla_rapoport (local densities giving its heights) + genesis_kudla_program (global generating-series framework) + genesis_gross_kohnen (weight-3/2 antecedent).
(= (arithmetic-theta-lift $V) (theta-form (arithmetic-chow-group $V) (generating-series (lambda ($T) (arithmetic-special-cycle $V $T)))))
(= (arithmetic-theta-modular $V) (implies (arithmetic-theta-lift $V) (modular-form (weight (plus (div $n 2) 1)) (arithmetic-chow-coefficients $V))))
(= (arithmetic-theta-height $V $T) (equal (arithmetic-degree (arithmetic-special-cycle $V $T)) (density-derivative (local-representation-density $T) (central-point))))